y  is 11 inches quite a bit smaller than  the 13-inch display on the MacBook Air  but it's got a few perks which I'll  mention in a minute but of course you  can get the 12 point 9 inch iPad pro for  $200 more if you'd like the benefit of  the Bridge Pro keyboard case is that  it's one of the only ones that allows  you to adjust the angle of the display  anywhere from 0 to 180 degrees even  we're sold in the MacBook Air now before  we get into comparing things like the  displays battery life and speakers I  want to give you guys a sneak peek at  one of the ways the iPad pro has greatly  improved in recent months and that's  software support I've personally used  Squarespace our sponsor for this video  to create a website from a wife's  cleaning business with no prior web  making experience at all and in the past  couple of months  the Squarespace app for iOS has been  greatly optimized for the iPad pro  allowing you to edit anything in  everything on your custom website that  includes changing settings like the  built-in SEO tools or customizing blocks  of text and images and easily  rearranging them with drag-and-drop  support so you no longer need a laptop  or a computer for web making because of  how simple it is on the iPad pro so  whether you choose to buy the MacBook or  the iPad pro to build a website for a  small business or literally anything  else go to squarespace.com for a free  trial and use our custom link below when  you're ready to launch - save 10% on  your first purchase of a website or  domain now getting into the featured  differences between the two the iPad  pros display is not only brighter than  the one on the MacBook Air but it's also  more color accurate with p-3 wide color  gamut support so it's a much better  choice for photo or video editing which  we'll get into in just a minute the iPad  pro also has the massive benefit of pro  motion technology which allows the  display to dynamically adjust from 24 to  120 Hertz based on the content 